    "finalPromptText": "I'm an undergrad working on a paper for my information design class about how Edward Tufte critiques \"chartjunk\" in his 1983 book The Visual Display of Quantitative Information — it's a classic data visualization reference that covers principles of statistical graphics. I need to analyze the specific examples and language Tufte uses when he introduces the concept of the data-ink ratio in the early chapters. Could you help me find the relevant passages where he defines and illustrates this idea? I have a copy from my university library but I want to make sure I'm not missing any key sections for my close reading.",
